<title>FRANCE: French auditors deliver audit to Jospin.</title>
<headline>French auditors deliver audit to Jospin.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French auditors asked by France's new Socialist-led government to draw up a report on the state of public finances delivered their audit to Prime Minister Lionel Jospin on Monday.</p>
<p>Jacques Bonnet and Philippe Nasse, members of the Court of Auditors, made no comment on arrival at Jospin's office.</p>
<p>Finance Minister Dominique Strauss-Kahn was due to present the results of the audit, along with measures to curb the state deficit, at a news conference at 0830 GMT.</p>
</text>
